From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] spi: stm32-qspi: use indirect reads on STM32F746 PoC

The STM32F746 no-MMU proof of concept intermittently faults when the CPU
copies directly from the QSPI memory aperture after the U-Boot-to-Linux
controller handoff.  Lowering the QSPI clock does not prevent the fault.

Decline creation of a direct-read mapping so the SPI-mem core uses its
supported spi_mem_exec_op() fallback.  The STM32 controller then performs
reads in CCR_FMODE_INDR through the FIFO instead of dereferencing the QSPI
aperture.  This is intentionally scoped to the board's QSPI Buildroot
configuration; it trades read performance for a reliable root filesystem.

Signed-off-by: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-stm32-qspi.c | 14 +-------------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-stm32-qspi.c b/drivers/spi/spi-stm32-qspi.c
index 35bc95a1a5bf..9d0ddb9df3e7 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-stm32-qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-stm32-qspi.c
@@ -504,19 +504,7 @@ static int stm32_qspi_exec_op(struct spi_mem *mem, const struct spi_mem_op *op)
 
 static int stm32_qspi_dirmap_create(struct spi_mem_dirmap_desc *desc)
 {
-	struct stm32_qspi *qspi = spi_controller_get_devdata(desc->mem->spi->master);
-
-	if (desc->info.op_tmpl.data.dir == SPI_MEM_DATA_OUT)
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
-
-	/* should never happen, as mm_base == null is an error probe exit condition */
-	if (!qspi->mm_base && desc->info.op_tmpl.data.dir == SPI_MEM_DATA_IN)
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
-
-	if (!qspi->mm_size)
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
-
-	return 0;
+	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 }
 
 static ssize_t stm32_qspi_dirmap_read(struct spi_mem_dirmap_desc *desc,
-- 
